{"nodes": [{"id": "how_long_until_dice_match_charts_iterations_per_simulation", "label": "Iterations per Simulation chart", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brag-output/brag-plan.md", "source_location": "L17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brag_output_brag_plan", "label": "brag-plan.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brag-output/brag-plan.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brag_output_brag_plan_brag_video", "label": "Brag video (23 s, 1920\u00d71080)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brag-output/brag-plan.md", "source_location": "L35", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brag_output_brag_plan_serious_science_for_stupid_questions", "label": "Serious science for stupid questions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brag-output/brag-plan.md", "source_location": "L7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The comedy is the gap between a silly question and absurd rigor, so the film plays it straight: every number is real and the numbers are the jokes."}, {"id": "brag_output_brag_plan_yc_parody_preset", "label": "yc-parody tone preset", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brag-output/brag-plan.md", "source_location": "L31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hard cuts, one claim per beat and zero jokes in the copy; the corporate-warm bed and lab-report seriousness make the dice statistics funny on their own."}, {"id": "brag_output_brag_plan_seaborn_whitegrid_identity", "label": "Seaborn whitegrid visual identity", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brag-output/brag-plan.md", "source_location": "L39", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The repo has no CSS, so the palette comes from its seaborn whitegrid notebook charts and terminal; the notebook's #FF0000 reference line becomes matplotlib tab:red #D62728 to pass WCAG AA as text."}, {"id": "brag_output_brag_plan_journal_serif_typography", "label": "STIX Two Text + IBM Plex Mono typography", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brag-output/brag-plan.md", "source_location": "L45", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "STIX Two Text is the scientific-journal typeface, so headlines read like a paper title; it replaced IBM Plex Sans, which is not bundled, and journal serif plus instrument mono is a stronger register switch."}, {"id": "brag_output_brag_plan_music_cue_locks", "label": "Music cue locks (6.34 / 9.50 / 12.65 s)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brag-output/brag-plan.md", "source_location": "L57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At most three hard locks (terminal cut-in, counter lock, 8,738 callout) with other cues as soft bias; cues bias timing but never drive visible pulsing, and there is no audio-reactive treatment because stillness sells the seriousness."}, {"id": "brag_output_brag_plan_motion_matched_sfx", "label": "Motion-matched sparse SFX", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brag-output/brag-plan.md", "source_location": "L65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At most seven cue moments, each matched to an on-screen gesture (dice, keys, counter lock, spike, stamp, logo bell); no SFX under readable headlines or on every terminal line, and nothing louder than the bed except the hook dice and the logo hit."}, {"id": "brag_output_brag_plan_scene_1_the_question", "label": "Scene 1 \u2014 The question", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brag-output/brag-plan.md", "source_location": "L71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brag_output_b